    "created_at": "2016-10-19T08:11:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-19T08:11:58Z",
    "body": "For the \"click in progress flag\": I'm able to reproduce the existence with `click()` clicks, but other kinds of click produce different results. `dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\"click\"))` clicks appear unbounded in both Firefox and Chrome (they have some recursion limit, but it's a lot more than one).\n\nMouse clicking `<input type=checkbox onclick='w(0);document.querySelector(\"input\").click()'>` results in it happening twice, so the flag is not shared between \"normal\" clicks and `click()` clicks.\n\nMouse click the first checkbox in `<input type=checkbox onclick='w(0);document.querySelectorAll(\"input\")[1].click()'><input type=checkbox onclick=w(1);document.querySelector(\"input\").click()>` results in 0 1 0 so again it seems like the flag is not shared.\n\nHowever, keyboard clicking, as you indicated, is different in Chrome. If you space bar the checkbox Chrome does share the flag. Firefox does not. I think Firefox is somewhat more reasonable in restricting the special case to just `click()`.\n\n@smaug---- @dtapuska?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
