    "created_at": "2016-10-19T18:28:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-19T18:28:01Z",
    "body": "> What guidance does it contain though? That a mouse click fires a click? UI events already says that.\n\nUpon re-reviewing, I guess you are right. The spec previously gave some guidance on how things should behave differently between mouse clicking and keyboard activation. However, the differences are basically about the canvas re-routing and nearest activatable element, which are now covered elsewhere.\n\n---\n\nThanks for putting the click() flag back. Unfortunately I guess it's not really possible to create non-manual tests to ensure it's _only_ used for click(). But maybe we can turn your examples into a manual test, and file bugs.\n\n---\n\nSo, this LGTM now \\o/. I guess maybe we should do the consistency name change first (thanks ^_^). And we should create a commit message that does mention some of the more substantial changes. I guess the biggest so far is moving click-in-progress to click() only?\n",
